WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.112
Choose the type based on meaning.

00:00:02.112 --> 00:00:05.917
If only the calendar day matters, DATE may be enough.

00:00:05.917 --> 00:00:11.582
If you need a local date and time without global time-zone meaning, TIMESTAMP may fit.

00:00:11.582 --> 00:00:15.967
If the value represents an instant, use TIMESTAMPTZ.

00:00:15.967 --> 00:00:19.397
If the value is duration, use INTERVAL.

00:00:19.397 --> 00:00:24.747
Remember that storage precision and analytical grain are separate decisions.

00:00:24.747 --> 00:00:27.907
Choose temporal types based on meaning.

00:00:27.907 --> 00:00:31.407
DATE is for calendar dates without time of day.

00:00:31.407 --> 00:00:36.257
TIMESTAMP stores a date and time without a time-zone interpretation.

00:00:36.257 --> 00:00:42.622
TIMESTAMPTZ represents an instant in time and is usually safer for events that cross regions or

00:00:42.622 --> 00:00:44.524
daylight-saving changes.
